rm","postgresql","react-native","sap","sap-hana","sqlite","sqlserver","typeorm","typescript","websql"],"visibility":"public","forks":6469,"open_issues":540,"watchers":36125,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Issue description\n\nstringified IDs for where-in clause causes a single query plan for each query\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nI would expect that value's injected in the query use query parameters and not use string interpolation. This appears to be the default behavior. However, an exception was added to appease sqlite's lower 1000 parameter limit in #190. \n\n### Actual Behavior\n\nString interpolation of query values into the query instead of using query parameters if all IDs are numbers.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate two related entities, fill each with records and query using relations in query builder or find() and notice that the where includes parameterized and numerical inline arguments. \n\n### My Environment\n\n| Dependency          | Version  |\r\n| ---                 | ---      |\r\n| Operating System    |  N/A     |\r\n| Node.js version     | v20.12.0 |\r\n| Typescript version  | 4.9.5 |\r\n| TypeORM version     | 0.3.10  |\r\n\n\n### Additional Context\n\nhttps://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/blob/e7649d2746f907ff36b1efb600402dedd5f5a499/src/query-builder/SelectQueryBuilder.ts#L3526-L3533\r\n\r\nThis is one of the locations where these IDs are injected. Manually setting areAllNumbers to false solves the problem for my use case, however that may not be desired behavior for some users.\n\n### Relevant Database Driver(s)\n\n- [ ] aurora-mysql\n- [ ] aurora-postgres\n- [ ] better-sqlite3\n- [ ] cockroachdb\n- [ ] cordova\n- [ ] expo\n- [ ] mongodb\n- [ ] mysql\n- [ ] nativescript\n- [ ] oracle\n- [ ] postgres\n- [ ] react-native\n- [ ] sap\n- [ ] spanner\n- [X] sqlite\n- [ ] sqlite-abstract\n- [ ] sqljs\n- [X] sqlserver\n\n### Are you willing to resolve this issue by submitting a Pull Request?\n\nYes, I have the time, but I don't know how to start. I would need guidance.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/10810/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/10810/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/comments/3509592812","html_url":"https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/issues/190#issuecomment-3509592812","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/190","id":3509592812,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAyVBJc7RMCLs","user":{"login":"54keesh","id":88324118,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MzI0MTE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88324118?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/54keesh","html_url":"https://github.com/54keesh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/54keesh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/54keesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/54keesh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/54keesh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/54keesh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/54keesh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/54keesh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/54keesh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/54keesh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-10T06:10:06Z","updated_at":"2025-11-10T06:10:06Z","body":"As far as the sqlite limits are concerned, [docs](https://sqlite.org/limits.html) says the following:\n\n> To prevent excessive memory allocations, the maximum value of a host parameter number is SQLITE_MAX_VARIABLE_NUMBER, which de